@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white

title Notification method selection at startup

actor Administrator
participant "External configuration" as Config
participant "NotificationChannelsConfig\n(setup composition)" as Setup
participant "NotificationChannelComposition" as Composition
participant SMSNotificationService as SMS
participant EmailNotificationService as Email
participant WebhookNotificationService as Webhook
participant LendingServiceImpl as Lending
participant NotificationPreferenceService as Preferences

Administrator -> Config : Set enabled notification channels\n(by identifier) before startup

Setup -> Setup : Register installed channels\n(identifier -> supplier)
Setup -> Config : Read channel identifier list
Config --> Setup : Configured value
Setup -> Composition : enabledChannels(identifiers)
Composition -> Composition : Parse and validate list

alt Invalid configuration
  Composition --> Setup : Exception (empty list,\nunknown or repeated identifier)
  note right of Setup
    Application startup fails.
    Error is reported in application logs.
  end note
else Valid configuration
  opt SMS channel enabled
    Composition -> SMS ** : supplier creates SMSNotificationService
  end
  opt Email channel enabled
    Composition -> Email ** : supplier creates EmailNotificationService
  end
  opt Webhook channel enabled
    Composition -> Webhook ** : supplier creates WebhookNotificationService
  end
  Composition --> Setup : Enabled channels, in configured order
  note over Setup,Composition
    A missing delivery setting of an enabled channel
    also stops startup; disabled channels need none.
  end note
  Setup -> Lending : Inject enabled instances\n(typed as NotificationService)
  Setup -> Preferences : Inject enabled instances\n(the set readers may choose from)
  note over Setup,Preferences
    Only enabled implementations are instantiated;
    disabled channels send 0 notifications.
    LendingServiceImpl depends only on NotificationService.
    Configuration changes require a restart.
  end note
end

@enduml
